Negative control for the TRACKS-NAME-A-MODULE law (`R6-37`).

Serves one module's committed playlist to every name asked for, so a declaration
tracking a module this seam does not reach plays somebody else's scenarios
instead of staying Live-only. The channel still looks like a module name; what
is withdrawn is the seam actually answering for that module.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the corpus-source spec — a module the seam does not reach resolves to no
track source at all.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/corpus.source.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/force/corpus.source.ts
